  "title": "SEC allows a limited tokenized-stock exemption through 2031",
  "question": "What did the SEC's effective Tokenized NMS Stock Innovation Exemption authorize, and which venue, issuer, record, liquidity, custody, clearing, settlement and token-selection gates remain?",
  "bluf": "On September 17, 2026 the SEC issued a live five-year order letting approved participants trade tokenized versions of listed stocks through automated pools on public blockchains. No such venue is running yet, and custody, clearing and settlement are left to others.",
  "evidence_cutoff": "2026-09-17T09:46:00-04:00",
  "evidence_cutoff_note": "The controlling 60-page order, docket, release and commissioner statements were checked on issue morning. The same-day 24-hour-trading roundtable had not yet begun. No operating TSV was established in the reviewed sources.",
  "use_note": "Effective exemption is not live operation. Require the TSV notice, 30-day clock, issuer process, product and pair identification, contract addresses, custody and settlement arrangements, and observed liquidity before carrying an operating or token-demand claim.",
